        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-787",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "CWE-787 - Out-of-bounds Write\nVulnerability: Heap Buffer Off-by-one Overflow in buffer_write\nDescription: A heap buffer overflow vulnerability exists in the buffer_write function in utils.c\ndue to an off-by-one error in the bounds checking logic. The function uses an\nincorrect comparison operator (>) instead of (>=) when validating the index parameter\nagainst the buffer size. This allows writing one byte beyond the allocated heap buffer.\n\nFor a buffer of size N, valid indices are 0 to N-1, but the current implementation\naccepts index N, causing a write at buf->buf[N] which is one byte past the end of\nthe allocated region. This vulnerability is triggered in fd-exhaustion-harness.c when\nspecific arithmetic constraints are met and buffer_write is called with an index\nequal to the buffer size (300).\n\nThe vulnerability can lead to heap memory corruption, potential control-flow hijacking,\ndenial of service, or corruption of adjacent heap data structures.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
